---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import PasswordGate from '../components/PasswordGate.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Approach — Robert Westwood">
	<PageTitle>My Approach To Design</PageTitle>
	<PasswordGate>
		<section class="approach container">
			<p class="copy intro">
				I see design as a strategic process for solving complex problems and building positive
				relationships between people and the products they use. It provides users with the
				comprehension and control to meet their needs today, while keeping an eye on tomorrow.
				The true value of design lives equally in the final product and the collaborative
				journey to create it.
			</p>
			<div class="grid">
				<div>
					<h2>Design is a craft</h2>
					<p class="copy">
						Great design requires sweating the small stuff without losing sight of the big
						picture. It is part detective work and part strategic thinking, placing user
						insights at the center of the creative process to deliver experiences that truly
						resonate.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h2>It is an inclusive team sport</h2>
					<p class="copy">
						A collaborative process brings teams together around a shared understanding of
						the problem space. Designers must act as orchestrators across Product,
						Engineering, and Architecture disciplines. When everyone is empowered to
						participate regardless of their role, it breaks down corporate silos, fuels
						alignment, and drives teams to take shared ownership of the solution.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h2>It is the connective tissue</h2>
					<p class="copy">
						Beyond crafting user experiences, applying design best practices improves how
						teams collaborate. It helps them navigate changing requirements and the unknown
						with agility and clarity, creating a cohesive environment across all
						disciplines.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h2>Design is accelerated by AI</h2>
					<p class="copy">
						The industry is moving faster than ever, and static deliverables are no longer
						enough. By embracing artificial intelligence workflows and prototyping directly
						in code, we can turn abstract concepts into tangible solutions rapidly.
						Integrating these tools accelerates project timelines and keeps teams ahead of
						the technology curve.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h2>It's a strategic business driver</h2>
					<p class="copy">
						Transforming complex systems is the mechanism, but driving enterprise value is
						the outcome. Design architecture must directly advance primary business goals
						and market differentiation. Every design decision should be a calculated
						investment that yields measurable returns and supports the broader product
						strategy.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h2>We must always revisit the why</h2>
					<p class="copy">
						User expectations and market demands constantly evolve, requiring us to
						challenge assumptions and embrace change. Staying strictly aligned with
						validated user problems keeps the work purposeful, but we must equally pressure
						test our ideas against business goals. A successful solution must seamlessly
						bridge the gap between what users need and what drives the business forward.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</PasswordGate>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.approach {
		padding-bottom: var(--space-section);
	}
	/* Copy: body text style shared by the intro and the quadrant paragraphs */
	.copy {
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		font-weight: 300;
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 48rem;
		margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
	}
	.grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		gap: var(--space-12) var(--gutter);
	}
	.grid h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		line-height: var(--leading-snug);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}
	.grid .copy {
		color: var(--color-muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
